# No rustc for a sanitized run (`asan/run.sh` puts this directory first on PATH).  loft asks
# `rustc --version` when it sums up a test run; every program loft starts inherits the
# sanitizer's runtime (LD_PRELOAD), and the real rustc never answers under it, so the run
# would hang after its last test.  The run is on the interpreter and needs no rustc.
exit 127
